Doumi is an intelligent file organizer that watches your folders and
automatically organizes files using rules you define -- like Hazel for
macOS, but native on Linux and BSD.

Features:
  - Real-time file watching via kqueue
  - Cron-based scheduled scans
  - Rich condition system (name, extension, date, size, MIME type, kind)
  - Actions: move, copy, rename, trash, delete, archive, notify, run scripts
  - GTK4 + libadwaita graphical rule editor
  - CLI for scripting and automation
  - Unix domain socket IPC between daemon and client
  - SQLite-backed action logging

